    "reading": [
      "Condition standardization wins clearly by CV where there are six operating conditions (FD002 16.57 vs 17.24, FD004 15.76 vs 16.58) and ties where there is one (FD001, FD003), as expected: for a single condition it is an affine rescaling, which trees ignore.",
      "Test RMSE: FD001 18.18, FD002 27.51, FD003 19.32, FD004 29.20; each constant baseline is 43-55. Multi-condition subsets stay hardest for a per-row gradient-boosting model; published deep sequence models report lower errors, and no sequence baseline was built here.",
      "FD003 differed from the local rehearsal (19.32 vs 20.56): Spark and pandas features differ by ~1e-12, which changed the CV winner. The same sensitivity as v3 vs v2; Gold features are the source of truth.",
      "FD001 in the benchmark (condition set, validation 14.99) is not a candidate for promotion: only cmapss_train registers, and only on the Gold feature contract."
